From: Nova <361320585+q2-nova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:24:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Follow cfg80211 API changes through Linux 7.3

The 6.9 channel-switch and 6.12 CAC helpers come from Stane1983's
rtl8733BS-aml tree (github.com/Stane1983/rtl8733BS-aml), applied
unchanged to this identical vendor release.

Further changes, each checked against the tagged release's
include/net/cfg80211.h, use thin forwarders so the vendor operations
stay unchanged:
- 6.13: set_monitor_channel receives the net_device.
- 6.14: get_tx_power receives link_id.
- 6.17: set_wiphy_params, set_tx_power and get_tx_power receive radio_idx.
- 7.1: key and station operations, cfg80211_new_sta() and
  cfg80211_del_sta() use the wireless_dev.
- 7.3: remain_on_channel and mgmt_tx receive the cookie cfg80211
  assigned; the driver reports that cookie instead of generating one.
  rx_addr is only set for drivers advertising ROC_ADDR_FILTER.
---
